Z||000002||BroCar 87||05-13-2000||10:05 PM||||HAHA... Sorry about that Cooter, I didn't know it was a touchy subject. I am still new to the FIERO FANATIC-ISM.<BR>I was just wondering cause I know how people are about Turbo's and all.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wannabe||05-13-2000||11:48 PM||||Everybody seems to forget that there was a turbo 2.0L offered by Pontiac in the Sunbird in the late '80's. It was rated about 165hp and 175lb-ft of torque. A 2.0 turbo with intercooler should easily be good for 250hp without overly compromising reliablity. These engines came with an aluminum head and the Getrag 5 spd. I believe they are based on the 2.2 currently offered in the Cavalier/Sunbird. Sounds like it would be a great swap for a 4 cyl Fiero (or maybe even a six for that matter) It is surprising that in all of the converstions about engine swaps for Fieros, this one never seems to be mentioned.||||reg||1
